  "steps": [
   "The scheduler starts the batch after XD12 has finished successfully (job chain XD12 -> XD11 -> XD08). Write LOG1.",
   {
    "text": "Select the rows of TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CANCEL_PRE that are crossdock lines and not yet processed:",
    "children": [
     "Crossdock line: the same unique key (CUSTOMER_CD + CUSTOMER_ORDER_NO + ORDER_DT + ORDER_TIME + DESTINATION_CD + DETAILED_ITEM_NO + SERIAL_NO) exists in TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE (status 7 data of the previous XD08 run).",
     "Not processed: no record in TB_R_CROSSDOCK_CANCEL_RESULT with the same unique key and ORDER_STATUS_DT."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "For each line, compute:",
    "children": [
     "LINE_QTY = ORDER_STATUS_QTY of the line in TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE; CANCEL_QTY = ORDER_STATUS_QTY of the status 2 row.",
     "QTY_IN_ASN = sum of QTY of the rows of the line in TB_R_INSTRUCTION with ASN_NO filled.",
     "OPEN_QTY = sum of QTY of the rows of the line in TB_R_INSTRUCTION without ASN_NO (mapped by [Create ASN], not submitted)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Judge the result (see Result Rule):",
    "children": [
     "CANCELLED: CANCEL_QTY <= LINE_QTY - QTY_IN_ASN, with or without hold (HOLD_FLAG is only recorded). Write LOG3.",
     "CONFLICT: CANCEL_QTY > LINE_QTY - QTY_IN_ASN (part of the cancelled qty is already in a submitted ASN). Write LOG4."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Release the open mapping of the line (all results):",
    "children": [
     "Delete the rows of the line in TB_R_INSTRUCTION without ASN_NO. A Case List still open for these rows can no longer be submitted (the submit fails and the user creates the ASN again).",
     "Reduce MAPPED_QTY in TB_R_PRA_DAILY_ORDER_MAPPED by the qty of the deleted rows, per PO part.",
     "Set PO_MAPPED_FLAG = 'N' on the line in TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE when no row of the line is left in TB_R_INSTRUCTION.",
     "Rows with ASN_NO (submitted ASN) are never changed."
    ]
   },
   "Insert the result in TB_R_CROSSDOCK_CANCEL_RESULT (RELEASED_QTY = OPEN_QTY, ASN_NO for CONFLICT). Commit per line: an error stops only this line (LOG5), which is processed again by the next run.",
   "More lines: back to step 3. Else write LOG2 (counts per result). Exit."
  ]
 },
