 "func_desc_layout": "full",
 "func_desc": [
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "marker": "-",
   "level": 0,
   "items": [
    "NSP never cancels a customer order and has no Cancel ASN. G-TOPAS cancels the order (status 2); this batch only applies the cancel to the crossdock data of NSP.",
    "Normal case (CANCELLED): G-TOPAS cancels qty that is not yet in a submitted ASN. The line may or may not be on hold in NSP (HOLD_FLAG is only recorded). The released PO qty is taken by the next orders in the next XD09 run (FIFO).",
    "Qty already in a submitted ASN should not be cancelled. How this is prevented (G-TOPAS check, SOP or feedback of the ASN data to G-TOPAS) is to be discussed; until then XD11 detects it as CONFLICT.",
    "CONFLICT: part of the cancelled qty is already in a submitted ASN (case shipped). The ASN stays as it is. The D/S team handles the case at receiving in G-TOPAS: allocate it to an open order with the same destination, otherwise move it to warehouse stock (refer prototype menu Cancel Order Simulation).",
    "TB_R_CROSSDOCK_CANCEL_RESULT is the exception list for the D/S team (RESULT = CONFLICT); a screen for it is not in this scope (TBC). The messages are also in the Log (Log Monitoring).",
    "Option not in this draft (TBC): keep the released PO qty of a CONFLICT blocked until the D/S team closes the conflict, to avoid over-supply when the shipped case is allocated to another order before the next XD08 run.",
    "Open points: how a cancel of qty already in an ASN is prevented; design of the H0253 replicate table (insert / update with status 7, 6, 2 instead of two full-replace tables); partial cancel in G-TOPAS (split SERIAL_NO or qty change); one customer order line in more than one ASN; content of the case label."
   ]
  }
 ],
